{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PictureInPictureCapable"},{"kind":"text","text":" : AnyObject"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The runtime’s default is to drive ","type":"text"},{"code":"AVPictureInPictureController","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" against the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"content ","type":"text"},{"code":"AVPlayerLayer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it discovers in the integrator’s view hierarchy.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"That works for players that keep one layer alive across source changes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(AVPlayer: the SDK swaps the ITEM on the same player), and breaks for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"players that rebuild their internal pipeline on a source change: THEOplayer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"replaces its internal AVPlayer\/layer when ","type":"text"},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is assigned, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"discovered layer dies, and AVKit closes the window at the exact moment the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SDK lends the content player to the ad. Measured on the iOS e2e fleet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(catalog-pip, SDK 0.50.0-beta.500): the window opened before the break and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closed at ","type":"text"},{"code":"adbreakbegin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with the ad playing full-screen in the main","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"window instead of inside it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Such players expose their own picture-in-picture facility with the missing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"piece — THEOplayer retains the window across source changes when the host"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constructs it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PiPConfiguration(retainPresentationModeOnSourceChange: true)"},{"type":"text","text":" — but only if the window is driven through THAT facility. This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol is how an adapter hands the SDK that steering wheel; the renderer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prefers it over its own controller whenever the content adapter conforms."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All three members are called on the main thread (the renderer is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":"); the change handler must likewise be invoked on the main"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thread, for every transition — including viewer-driven ones (the system UI"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can dismiss the window at any time), which is the whole reason the handler"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exists: the break format follows what is actually on screen."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Optional capability a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PlayerAdapter"},{"type":"text","text":" implements when its player owns"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"picture-in-picture natively."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PictureInPictureCapable\/isPictureInPicture()","doc